{"id":"nd8b00d2c90","headline":"Ringgit closes higher against US dollar despite fed rate hike expectations","summary":"The ringgit closed higher against the US dollar on Friday, driven by bargain-hunting activity. The move came despite expectations of further US interest rate hikes.","why":"The ringgit is Malaysia's currency, and its exchange rate with the US dollar affects import costs, foreign investment flows and returns on ringgit assets. US rate expectations are a key driver of dollar strength across emerging-market currencies.","category":"markets","event_type":"macro-data","importance":2,"flag":null,"market_moving":false,"location":{"place":"Kuala Lumpur","country":"Malaysia","lat":3.139,"lon":101.687,"region":"asia"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"The Star","url":"https://www.thestar.com.my/business/business-news/2026/09/25/ringgit-closes-higher-against-us-dollar-despite-fed-rate-hike-expectations"},"sources":[{"name":"The Star","url":"https://www.thestar.com.my/business/business-news/2026/09/25/ringgit-closes-higher-against-us-dollar-despite-fed-rate-hike-expectations"}],"published_at":"2026-09-25T19:08:00Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-12T00:21:16Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"7b9e54bd3e5e524c","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-12T00:21:16Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-09-25T19:08:00Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-09-25T12:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"MY","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/banknotes-money-4122079.jpg","alt":"banknotes money (illustration)","credit":"_Alicja_","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/banknotes-the-currency-in-poland-4122079/"}}